    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_614820f",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Three Things That Actually Make A Difference",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "heading_size_mobile": 32,
            "heading_line_height": 1,
            "heading_color": "#121212",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 50,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 30,
            "column_1_text": "<p><strong>Moisturize first. </strong>It sounds almost too simple, but applying an unscented or lightly scented moisturizer before you spray is one of the most effective things you can do. We tested this with all the scientific rigor of two people sharing an apartment: same person, same fragrance, two consecutive mornings. On dry skin, the scent was mostly gone by mid-morning. On moisturized skin, it was still going strong at 4pm. The difference was hard to miss. It costs nothing extra and takes about twelve seconds.</p><p><strong>Apply to pulse points. </strong>Wrists are the starting point, but go further. Neck, inside of elbows, behind the knees. These spots generate heat throughout the day, and heat is what activates fragrance and keeps it going. The most common mistake is rubbing your wrists together after spraying, which almost everyone does, and which grinds down the top notes. You are not locking the scent in. You are doing the opposite. Let them dry.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p><strong>Do not spray your clothes instead of your skin. </strong>It feels logical in the moment, especially with delicate fabrics. But fragrance is designed to work with your skin chemistry. On fabric, you get the scent but none of the warmth, the development, or the depth that makes a great perfume worth wearing. You will smell like a fitting room rather than a person. There is a difference.<br/><br/></p>",
            "body_size": 22,
            "body_size_mobile": 14,
            "body_line_height": 1.6,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 60,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1000,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>The Concentration Question: EDT, EDP, And Why It Matters</p>",
            "heading_size": 60,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>EDP (Eau de Parfum) contains a higher concentration of fragrance oil than EDT (Eau de Toilette), which means it lasts longer and carries further. The <a href=\"/collections/women\" title=\"Women\">best perfume for women</a>, and the top perfumes for women overall, tend to sit in the EDP range if you want all-day wear without having to reapply before lunch.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "",
            "subheading_size": 60,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>A lot of people assume that longer-lasting means a stronger or heavier scent. It does not. Concentration affects longevity, not character. An EDP version of a light, fresh fragrance is still light and fresh. It just stays that way for longer, which is the whole point of investing in it. <a href=\"/collections/unisex\" title=\"Unisex\">Luxury unisex perfumes</a> are worth considering here too. Long-lasting perfume in EDP concentration can be outstanding, and regularly gets passed over by anyone shopping strictly by gender.</p><p></p><p>The best cologne for men, whether you are shopping men’s fragrances from a luxury fragrance store or browsing inspired options online in the US, will outlast an EDT when the concentration is right. The bottle may look identical. How long it lasts absolutely will not.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 22,
            "bottom_text_color": "#000000",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.6
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "custom_css": [],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_jgTJWD": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_19f144a",
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "Timeless Grace",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 300,
            "line_2_text": "vs",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "Coco Mademoiselle by Chanel:",
            "line_3_alignment": "right",
            "line_3_offset": -40,
            "body_text": "<p>Coco Mademoiselle is the benchmark for a certain kind of feminine fragrance. Clean, grown-up, and immediately recognisable. It has been the top-selling women's perfume in the UK and US for years. The EDP retails at around $160 for 100ml and it earns that position consistently.</p><p><strong>Timeless Grace</strong> opens with the same fresh orange and bergamot, develops through jasmine and rose, and settles into a warm patchouli base that wears throughout the day. The comparison test here produced the closest result of the three: on dry-down, both fragrances sat in the same warm, clean territory. The original has a very slight additional depth in the base that reflects the higher concentration of raw materials, but it is a difference you would only notice if you were specifically looking for it.<br/><br/>At around $20 versus $160, Timeless Grace makes a compelling case for anyone who loves the Coco Mademoiselle profile but wants to wear it every day without the creeping sense that they should be saving it for something more significant.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 44,
            "line_2_size": 85,
            "line_3_size": 44,
            "body_size": 22,
            "line_2_margin_top": 30,
            "line_3_margin_top": 4,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 1000,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#121212"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7"
      ],
      "disabled": true,
      "name": "Staggered typography",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "17786893180b60ea14": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_c88e324",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1200,
            "left_column_width": 40,
            "right_column_width": 60,
            "column_gap": 40,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "One Thing Worth Knowing About Inspired Fragrances",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "mobile_heading_size": 40,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_indent": 10,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 40,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/One_thing_worth_knowing_1.png",
            "image_max_width": 600,
            "heading_image_gap": 4,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 25,
            "body_text": "<p>This comes up all the time. Do inspired fragrances actually last as long as the originals? For anyone exploring <a href=\"https://scentspired.com/\" title=\"https://scentspired.com/\">luxury inspired perfumes</a>, it comes down to concentration and formula quality. That is it. Whether it is inspired or original does not change the answer.</p><p>A well-made EDP from a luxury inspired perfume collection will outlast a lower-concentration EDT from a designer house. What you are paying for with the designer version is largely the bottle, the packaging, and the quiet confidence that someone in Milan approved the font. The actual fragrance inside is where a quality inspired alternative, whether you buy perfume online or through a fragrance store, performs just as well. That is the part that counts.</p><p>Once you know these things, you cannot unknow them. That is either very useful or a little inconvenient the next time you are standing in Sephora being handed a tester strip. The full Scentspired perfume collection, covering luxury inspired perfumes for women, men, and unisex, is right here whenever you are ready to shop.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 24,
            "mobile_body_size": 16,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 30,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 10,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_top": 100,
            "padding_bottom": 100,
            "horizontal_padding": 40,
            "mobile_padding_top": 60,
            "mobile_padding_bottom": 60,
            "mobile_horizontal_padding": 20,
            "mobile_gap": 30
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4"
      ],
